<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mithridates I of Parthia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 171–132 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> · Also known as Mithridates I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mithridates I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthia">Parthia</a> from about 171 to 132 BCE and is regarded as the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a> as a major power. He conquered Media and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>. His victories reduced the Seleucids to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and established Parthia as the dominant Iranian state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mithridates-i-of-parthia.jpg" alt="Mithridates I of Parthia" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Mithradates_I_of_Parthia,_Seleucia_mint.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The small regional kingdom became a major imperial power under <b>Mithridates I</b> (r. c. 171–132 BCE), who conquered Media and, around 141 BCE, the Seleucid heartland of Mesopotamia.</blockquote><a href="/empire/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Mithridates I of Parthia</b> exploited the succession struggles that followed Antiochus IV's death to conquer Media (c. 148–147 BCE) and Mesopotamia (141 BCE), capturing Seleucia-on-Tigris, the empire's eastern capital, and in 138 BCE taking the Seleucid king Demetrius II prisoner.</blockquote><a href="/empire/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a>. Died in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p></section>
